      "problem": "Given that $P(F|G)=0.5,$ $P(F)=0.25,$ and $P(G)=0.3,$ compute $P(G|F).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G|F) & =\\frac{P(F|G)P(G)}{P(F)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.5)(0.3)}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.15}{0.25} \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
